# Shell scripts MUST be LF, always.
#
# install.sh was found on disk with CRLF line endings while the committed copy
# was LF — a Windows editor had rewritten it silently. `bash -n` refuses that
# file outright ("syntax error near unexpected token `|'"), so had it ever been
# committed and pulled onto an Ubuntu server, the installer would not have run
# at all. The failure would have looked like a corrupt download, not an
# editor setting.
#
# `text eol=lf` makes git normalise on checkout regardless of the editor.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: these are read by Linux tooling.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
